      "title": "Setup required \u00b7 select models and a saved bundle",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Krea 2 Turbo Style Reference \u00b7 use a saved RefMod\n\n1. Run RefMod_Bake_Image_Families.json first, with model=krea2 and the matching VAE.\n2. The loaders name the exact checkpoint variant, text encoder and VAE this preset targets. Install those files or their matching precision variants.\n3. In Image RefMod Apply, select krea2/example_character (or your own bundle). Model is auto (from refmod). Leaving the picker on None stops execution until a bundle is chosen. Refresh node definitions (R) after creating a bundle if it is not listed.\n4. Edit the prompt, then queue. References condition the result; identity, style and edit fidelity depend on the model and task.\n\n## Settings\n\nSampler values are starting points, not universal presets. Use the settings recommended for your exact checkpoint, especially for distilled models. Baked references must use the same VAE family as generation.\n\n## Required edit LoRA\n\nChoose a compatible reference-image edit LoRA in the connected model-only LoRA loader. Set edit_format on Apply to match how it was trained: ai-toolkit uses isolated/cached references; ai-toolkit (kv_cache off) uses uncached references. Moss-Image-Edit is MOSS-only. Use a current ComfyUI build with this model family's reference conditioning.\n\nThe Krea example uses krea2_style_reference.safetensors and Krea2 style reference format, matching the official Turbo style-reference blueprint. Its prompt is a description of the new image in the reference's style, not a promise of character identity preservation.\n\nOptional: combine refmod_2/refmod_3 from the SAME family. ref_strength sets how long image references are active, not their pixel amplitude."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# Krea 2 Turbo Style Reference \u00b7 use a saved RefMod\n\n1. Run RefMod_Bake_Image_Families.json first, with model=krea2 and the matching VAE.\n2. The loaders name the exact checkpoint variant, text encoder and VAE this preset targets. Install those files or their matching precision variants.\n3. In Image RefMod Apply, select krea2/example_character (or your own bundle). Model is auto (from refmod). Leaving the picker on None stops execution until a bundle is chosen. Refresh node definitions (R) after creating a bundle if it is not listed.\n4. Edit the prompt, then queue. References condition the result; identity, style and edit fidelity depend on the model and task.\n\n## Settings\n\nSampler values are starting points, not universal presets. Use the settings recommended for your exact checkpoint, especially for distilled models. Baked references must use the same VAE family as generation.\n\n## Required edit LoRA\n\nChoose a compatible reference-image edit LoRA in the connected model-only LoRA loader. Set edit_format on Apply to match how it was trained: ai-toolkit uses isolated/cached references; ai-toolkit (kv_cache off) uses uncached references. Moss-Image-Edit is MOSS-only. Use a current ComfyUI build with this model family's reference conditioning.\n\nThe Krea example uses krea2_style_reference.safetensors and Krea2 style reference format, matching the official Turbo style-reference blueprint. Its prompt is a description of the new image in the reference's style, not a promise of character identity preservation.\n\nOptional: combine refmod_2/refmod_3 from the SAME family. ref_strength sets how long image references are active, not their pixel amplitude."
      }
    },
